<Base title="Who we are" description="Who runs Curious about Islam, why, and how?" lang="en">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About Curious about Islam</h1>
    <p>Curious about Islam (궁금한 이슬람) is a guide made by Muslims living in Korea, for Koreans who are curious or worried about Islam. Instead of news headlines and rumours, we want to share honestly, in Korean, what Muslims actually believe and how they live.</p>

    <h2>Who makes it?</h2>
    <p class="notice">Team introductions are coming. (A Korean editor, Korean Muslim writers and the reviewing scholar will be introduced here.)</p>

    <h2>Our principles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No pressure.</strong> The goal is understanding, not conversion. We follow the teaching "There is no compulsion in religion" (Qur'an 2:256).</li>
      <li><strong>We listen to the worry first.</strong> Fear of Islam has its reasons. We acknowledge the concern before we answer it.</li>
      <li><strong>We show our sources.</strong> Qur'an and hadith are cited by chapter and verse; statistics and events by source.</li>
      <li><strong>We don't put down other religions.</strong> We state differences honestly and leave the judgement to the reader.</li>
      <li><strong>No politics.</strong> We take no position on particular countries, parties or international conflicts.</li>
      <li><strong>Reviewed before publishing.</strong> Every page should be reviewed by an Islamic scholar. Pages not yet reviewed are marked.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where does the funding come from?</h2>
    <p class="notice">Funding and support details will be published here in full.</p>

    <h2>Found a mistake?</h2>
    <p>If something is wrong or worded badly, please <a href="/en/ask/">tell us</a>. We will check, correct it, and note the correction.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
